                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5201a634-390d-3026-83e2-7aed8aff1081",
                        "entry_id": "d88ecfbf-c04a-3a0a-b3bf-5ce132995edd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to pall on, to become boring"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e83dcceb-aba2-45d1-aa6a-48031b88e3d6",
                                "sense_id": "5201a634-390d-3026-83e2-7aed8aff1081",
                                "text": "Рома́нтик сказа́л бы: я чу́вствую, что на́ши доро́ги начина́ют расходи́ться, а я про́сто говорю́, что мы друг дру́гу прие́лись. […] Душа́ моя́, э́то не беда́; то ли ещё на све́те приеда́ется!",
                                "translation": "A sentimentalist would say, \"I feel that our paths are beginning to part,\" but I will simply say that we're tired of each other. […] My dear soul, there's no great harm in that. One gets tired of much more than that in this life.",
                                "english": "A sentimentalist would say, \"I feel that our paths are beginning to part,\" but I will simply say that we're tired of each other. […] My dear soul, there's no great harm in that. One gets tired of much more than that in this life."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
